<title>USA: FOB Gulf Grain - Wheat down on slack exports.</title>
<headline>FOB Gulf Grain - Wheat down on slack exports.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Some wheat FOB values edged lower Tuesday in quiet trade as the market responded to a slack export market, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;There's just nothing in the wheat,&quot; said one Kansas City-based broker. &quot;There's some barley business around but that's about it.&quot;</p>
<p>Foreign wheat buyers were expected to continue to turn to Australia and Argentina for near-term purchases because of more favorable prices, dealers said.</p>
<p>Corn and soybean FOB values continued to find support from ongoing export business.</p>
<p>Some cash sources reported that demand for corn at the U.S. Gulf was solid Tuesday.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))  </p>
